<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy (UK) | Finance with Flow"
  description="How Finance with Flow uses cookies and web storage responsibly to support our website, and how you can manage your preferences."
  lastUpdated="10 September 2026"
  noindex={true}
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy applies to <strong>Finance with Flow Limited</strong> and our website, <a href="https://financewithflow.com">financewithflow.com</a>. It explains how we use cookies and related technologies in accordance with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR).
  </p>

  <p>
    This policy should be read alongside our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> and our <a href="/terms-conditions/">Terms and Conditions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Are Cookies and Local Storage?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files placed on your computer or mobile device by websites that you visit. They are widely used to make websites work more efficiently, provide secure browsing, and deliver reporting information to the website operator.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also make use of <strong>Local Storage</strong>, a standard modern web browser technology that allows our website to remember your consent choices locally on your device without sending that data back and forth to our servers on every page request.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We keep our use of cookies transparent, minimal, and secure. We categorise the technologies used on our website into three clear groups:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Strictly Necessary &amp; Functional Technologies:</strong> Essential for the site to function properly, navigate pages securely, and remember your cookie consent preferences. These cannot be disabled because the website cannot function reliably without them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics &amp; Performance Cookies:</strong> Used to understand how visitors interact with our website (such as which pages are visited most frequently and whether visitors encounter any errors). All analytics data is aggregated and anonymised with IP masking enabled. These cookies are only placed if you grant permission.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Marketing &amp; Campaign Attribution Cookies:</strong> Used to evaluate the performance of our marketing campaigns and understand how visitors reach our services. We do <em>not</em> run third-party advertising banners, nor do we sell user data to advertising brokers. These cookies are only activated if you grant consent.
    </li>
  </ol>

